@title Lab Result Routing
@subtitle Who is told, and when
@author Calder Valley Hospital laboratory informatics team
@date 2026-10-02

## Routing flow
diagram route dir=TB title="Routing flow"
route: verify "Result verified in lab system" svc
route: crit "Critical value?" decision
route: phone "Phone the ordering clinician" svc "urgent" focus
route: rb "Read-back confirmed within 15 minutes?" decision
route: logrb "Log the read-back" svc "urgent"
route: esc "Escalate to department head" svc "urgent"
route: flag "Flagged abnormal?" decision
route: inbox "Add to clinician inbox" svc "routine"
route: file "File without alert" svc "routine"
route: release "Release to patient portal" svc "routine"
route: verify -> crit
route: crit -> phone : yes
route: phone -> rb
route: rb -> logrb : yes
route: rb -> esc : no
route: esc -> logrb
route: crit -> flag : no
route: flag -> inbox : yes
route: flag -> file : no
route: inbox -> release
route: file -> release

!! Critical values need a phone call within 10 minutes of verification. Do not wait for the clinician inbox.

## Time limits
table = Step,Limit,Track; Phone call for a critical value,within 10 minutes of verification,Urgent; Read-back confirmation,within 15 minutes of the call,Urgent; Abnormal result review,in the clinician inbox within 1 business day,Routine; Routine result release,to the patient portal after 24 hours,Routine; Abnormal result hold,for 72 hours so the clinician can speak to the patient first,Routine

## Who is called
- Weekdays, 07:00 to 19:00: the ordering clinician.
- Nights and weekends: the covering physician, through the hospital operator.
- Department head: Dr. Naomi Eze.
